id=nemu_boot_autostart
name=Nemu Boot Guard
version=1.18
versionCode=19
author=Nemu
description=Auto-unbrick guard (3 failed boots): a verified clean shutdown or a user-requested root-side planned shutdown is not counted as a failed boot; watchdog/thermal reboots still count. v1.18 restores every Nemu-owned freeze state -- disable-user, hidden (pseudo-uninstall), suspend, disabled components, AppOps and standby buckets -- as soon as PackageManager answers at the early service stage (best-effort before the launcher), then verifies again after boot_completed; this covers unclean adb reboot/power loss and a frozen system app keeping the device on the boot screen. Normal/early passes are ownership-marker scoped; automatic rescue additionally restores Nemu's known target list but never scans arbitrary foreign suspensions.
